<button role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="r1" id="t-r1">How it works</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="r2" id="t-r2" tabindex="-1">Feasibility</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="r3" id="t-r3" tabindex="-1">Challenges</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="r4" id="t-r4" tabindex="-1">Benefits</button></div>
<div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="r1" aria-labelledby="t-r1"><ol class="flow"><li>An animal steps on the sensor plate.</li><li>A detection signal is generated.</li><li>The microcontroller processes the signal.</li><li>The railway warning signal activates (proposed red).</li><li>An approaching train is warned to slow down or stop.</li><li>The signal returns to green after safe crossing and clearance.</li></ol></div>
<div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="r2" aria-labelledby="t-r2" hidden><p>The concept relies on simple, well-understood parts: pressure sensors, a microcontroller for signal processing, and an amplifier. Solar-powered units let remote installations run without grid supply, which matters along forested rail stretches.</p><p style="margin:0">As a concept, it has not been installed on a live railway. Any real deployment would need authorised railway signalling integration.</p></div>
<div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="r3" aria-labelledby="t-r3" hidden><ul><li>False detection, for example from non-target animals or debris.</li><li>Sensor durability under heavy animal weight.</li><li>Weather protection for outdoor electronics.</li><li>Ongoing maintenance in remote locations.</li><li>Integration with authorised railway signalling systems.</li></ul></div>
<div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="r4" aria-labelledby="t-r4" hidden><p>Expected benefits, if developed and deployed:</p><ul><li>Fewer wildlife and train collisions, particularly involving elephants.</li><li>Safer railway operations.</li><li>Guided crossing zones that direct animals to predictable places.</li><li>A sustainable, solar-powered approach to environmental protection.</li></ul></div>
</div>
